-- title:
--   Word-independent factorisation of unramified unipotent twisted transversal integrals
-- statement:
--   Fix number fields $K$ and $L$ with $L/K$ Galois, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ over $K$ lies in the subgroup generated by the powers of $\sigma$ (the hypothesis `hgen`, i.e. $L/K$ is cyclic with generator $\sigma$). Let $D$ be an idele Galois descent datum for $L/K$: a homomorphism from $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ to the ring automorphisms of the adele ring $\mathbb{A}_L$, compatible with the algebra map $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$ and continuous in each automorphism; write $\sigma_D$ both for the induced ring automorphism `D.act σ` of $\mathbb{A}_L$ and for the induced group automorphism `unitsAct D σ` of $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$. Let $\nu_{Z_L}$ be a Haar measure on $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ and $\mu_K$ an additive Haar measure on $\mathbb{A}_K$.
--
--   Character and place data. $S_L$ is a finite set of finite places of $L$, and $\xi_L$ is a homomorphism from the full subgroup $\top$ of $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$. The hypothesis `hSL` requires every finite place $w$ of $L$ whose ramification index over the place of $K$ it lies under is $\neq 1$ to belong to $S_L$. The character hypotheses are: `hξc`, continuity of $z \mapsto \xi_L(z)$ as a complex-valued function; `hξt`, triviality of $\xi_L$ on the image of $L^\times$ under the map $L^\times \to \mathbb{A}_L^\times$; and `hξσ`, invariance $\xi_L(\sigma_D z_0) = \xi_L(z_0)$ for all $z_0$. Further, $S$ is a finite set of finite places of $K$, $\varphi_a$ a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the infinite adele ring of $L$, and $\varphi_S$ assigns to each finite place $v$ of $K$ a complex-valued function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$. $T$ is a further finite set of finite places of $K$ subject to `hT`: no place $w$ of $L$ lying over a place of $T$ belongs to $S_L$.
--
--   Word data. For each finite place $v$ of $K$ there are given a place $w_v =$ `ws v` of $L$ above $v$, a natural number $n_v =$ `ns v`, a family $r_{v,\bullet} =$ `rTs v` of elements of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$ indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}(n_v)$, and an element $z_v =$ `zs v` of $\mathrm{GL}_2(L_{w_v})$.
--
--   The finite set $S_\tau$ is pinned down by `hSτ`: a place $v$ lies in $S_\tau$ if and only if either $v \in S$ and $v \notin T$, or there is a place $w$ of $L$ above $v$ with ramification index over $v$ different from $1$.
--
--   Transversal data. There are a natural number $n$, reals $c_j$ for $j \in \mathrm{Fin}(n)$, measures $\tau_j$ on $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ for its Borel structure, measures $\tau^{\mathrm{fin}}_{j,v}$ on $(L \otimes_K K_v)^\times$ for each finite place $v$ of $K$, measures $\tau^{\mathrm{arch}}_{j,v}$ on $(\prod_{w \mid v} L_w)^\times$ for each infinite place $v$ of $K$, and units $\pi_{j,v} \in (L \otimes_K K_v)^\times$. Their hypotheses are: `hcpos`, $c_j > 0$; `hlev`, the set of $t$ with `ideleNorm L t` $\neq c_j$ (the norm being the modulus of the scaling action of $t$ on $\mathbb{A}_L$) is $\tau_j$-null; `hτfin`, each $\tau_j$ is finite on compact sets; `hτ0`, the complement of the saturated set $\{t : \forall v \notin S_\tau,\ \mathrm{semiLocalIdele}_v(t) \in U_v \cdot \mathrm{range}(\mathrm{includeUnits}_v)\}$ is $\tau_j$-null, where $U_v =$ `integralUnits K L v` is the unit group of the image of $\mathcal{O}_L \otimes \mathcal{O}_{K_v}$ in $L \otimes_K K_v$ and $\mathrm{semiLocalIdele}_v$ sends an idele to the unit determined by its finite part at the places above $v$; `hgood`, for $v \notin S_\tau$ the measure $\tau^{\mathrm{fin}}_{j,v}$ is a Haar measure of $(L \otimes_K K_v)^\times$ restricted to $U_v$ and normalised to total mass one; `hgood'`, for $v \notin S_\tau$ the complement of $U_v$ is $\tau^{\mathrm{fin}}_{j,v}$-null and $\tau^{\mathrm{fin}}_{j,v}(U_v) = 1$; `hbad`, for $v \in S_\tau$ the measure $\tau^{\mathrm{fin}}_{j,v}$ is the translate by $\pi_{j,v}$ of the push-forward to $(L \otimes_K K_v)^\times$ of a Haar measure on the norm-one subgroup `normOneUnits K L v` (the kernel of the valuation of the $K_v$-algebra norm); `harch`, each $\tau^{\mathrm{arch}}_{j,v}$ is the push-forward of a Haar measure on the archimedean norm-one subgroup `archNormOneUnits K L v`; and `hfac3`, the factorisation statement asserting that for every finite $S_f \supseteq S_\tau$ and all measurable families $f_v$ on $(L \otimes_K K_v)^\times$ and $g_v$ on $(\prod_{w\mid v} L_w)^\times$ with values in $[0,\infty]$, the lower integral over $\tau_j$ of the product of $\prod_{v \mid \infty} g_v(\mathrm{archSemiLocalIdele}_v(t))$, $\prod_{v \in S_f} f_v(\mathrm{semiLocalIdele}_v(t))$ and the indicator of the set of $t$ integral at all $v \notin S_f$ equals $\big(\prod_{v \mid \infty} \int g_v \, d\tau^{\mathrm{arch}}_{j,v}\big)\prod_{v \in S_f} \int f_v \, d\tau^{\mathrm{fin}}_{j,v}$.
--
--   Finally, $S_0$ is an arbitrary finite set of finite places of $K$.
--
--   Conclusion. There exist a finite set $S_x$ of finite places of $K$, functions $g_{L,j}$ on the infinite adele ring of $L$, functions $F_{j,v}$ on $L \otimes_K K_v$, and constants $c_T(v) \in \mathbb{C}$, such that:
--
--   1. $S \cup T \subseteq S_x$, $S_\tau \subseteq S_x$ and $S_0 \subseteq S_x$;
--
--   2. for every $j$, $g_{L,j}$ is continuous with compact support, and its transport $y \mapsto g_{L,j}((\mathrm{InfiniteAdeleRing.ringEquiv\_mixedSpace}\ L)^{-1}(y))$ to the mixed space of $L$ is $C^\infty$ over $\mathbb{R}$;
--
--   3. for every $j$ and every $v \in S_x$ with $v \notin T$, the function $F_{j,v}$ is locally constant with compact support;
--
--   4. for all functions $k_\bullet, j_\bullet$ from the finite places of $K$ to $\mathbb{N}$, every $\varphi$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$ and every $\varphi_f$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adele ring of $L$ such that `IsSemiLocalFactorization K L (S ∪ T)` holds for $\varphi$, $\varphi_a$, $\varphi_f$ and the semi-local family which at $v \in T$ is the word indicator $x \mapsto \sum_{\iota : \mathrm{Fin}(k_v) \to \mathrm{Fin}(n_v)} \mathbf{1}_{\mathrm{semiLocalIntegralSet}_v}\big((\mathrm{semiLocalComponent}_v(\mathrm{localEmbed}_{w_v}(\prod_m r_{v,\iota(m)} \cdot z_v^{\,j_v})))^{-1} x\big)$ and at $v \notin T$ is $\varphi_S(v)$ — that is: $\varphi_a$ is a smooth compactly supported function of the matrix entries at the infinite places, $\varphi_f$ is locally constant with compact support, each semi-local factor at $v \in S \cup T$ is locally constant with compact support, $\varphi_f(h)$ equals the product of the semi-local factors at $v \in S \cup T$ whenever $h$ is integral at all $v \notin S \cup T$ and vanishes otherwise, and $\varphi = (\varphi_a \circ \mathrm{glArch}) \cdot (\varphi_f \circ \mathrm{glFin})$ — the following three assertions hold.
--
--   (a) For every $v \in T$, the function $y \mapsto c_T(v) \cdot \mathrm{unipotentOrbitalFn}(K, L, \xi_L, v, w_v, n_v, r_{v,\bullet}, z_v, k_v, j_v)(y)$ on $L \otimes_K K_v$ is locally constant with compact support; here the orbital function is $\int_{(L\otimes_K K_v)^\times} \chi_v(\zeta) \int_{\mathrm{semiLocalIntegralSet}_v} \mathrm{wordIndicator}(\kappa^{-1}\, \mathrm{diag}_{\text{scalar}}(\zeta)\, n(y))\, d\kappa \, d\zeta$ against a Haar measure on $(L\otimes_K K_v)^\times$ and the semi-local Haar measure on $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$, with $\chi_v$ the product over the places $w$ of $L$ above $v$ of $\xi_L$ applied to the determinant of the Hecke generator attached to the $w$-component of $\zeta$.
--
--   (b) For every $j$, the function on the finite adele ring of $L$ obtained as the indicator of $\{x_f : \forall v \notin S_x,\ \mathrm{semiLocalEval}_v(x_f) \in \mathrm{semiLocalIntegers}_v\}$ times $\prod_{v \in S_x} h_v(\mathrm{semiLocalEval}_v(x_f))$, where $h_v$ is $y \mapsto c_T(v)\cdot \mathrm{unipotentOrbitalFn}(\dots)(y)$ for $v \in T$ and $F_{j,v}$ otherwise, is locally constant with compact support.
--
--   (c) For every $j$ and every adele $x \in \mathbb{A}_L$, putting
--    $$G_{t,k,\zeta}(x) = \varphi\big(k^{-1}\, n(x t^{-1})\, \mathrm{diag}(\sigma_D(t) t^{-1}, 1)\, \mathrm{scalar}(\sigma_D(\zeta))\, \sigma_D(k)\big),$$
--    with $n(\cdot)$ the upper unipotent matrix, $\mathrm{diag}(a,1)$ the image of $a$ under `diagOne`, $\mathrm{scalar}$ the central embedding of $\mathbb{A}_L^\times$ into $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_L)$, and $\sigma_D(k)$ the image of $k$ under the $\mathrm{GL}_2$-map induced by $\sigma_D$: first, the iterated lower integral $\int^- \int^- \int^- \|\xi_L(\zeta) G_{t,k,\zeta}(x)\|_e\, d\nu_{Z_L}(\zeta)\, dk\, d\tau_j(t)$ over $\zeta$, then $k$ against the Haar measure `maximalCompactHaar L` of the adelic maximal compact subgroup (those $k$ whose finite part is integral and whose archimedean components are row isometries), then $t$, is not $\infty$; and second,
--    $$\int \int \int \xi_L(\zeta)\, G_{t,k,\zeta}(x)\, d\nu_{Z_L}(\zeta)\, dk\, d\tau_j(t) = \mathbf{1}_{\mathrm{semiLocalIntegralOutside}(K,L,S_x)}(x)\; g_{L,j}(x_\infty) \prod_{v \in S_x} h_v(\mathrm{semiLocalEval}_v(x_f)),$$
--    where $x_\infty$ and $x_f$ are the infinite and finite parts of $x$, the indicator is that of the set of adeles integral at all semi-local places outside $S_x$, and $h_v$ is as in (b). In particular the set $S_x$, the archimedean factors $g_{L,j}$, the local factors $F_{j,v}$ and the constants $c_T$ are chosen before, hence independently of, the word data $k_\bullet, j_\bullet$ and of $\varphi, \varphi_f$.
--
--   This is the kernel half of the pointwise identification of the transversal pieces of the unipotent-type term in the twisted trace formula for $\mathrm{GL}(2)$ over a cyclic extension, at places unramified for the Hecke word data: the transversal, maximal-compact and central integrations are carried out first, producing a factorised expression whose $T$-factors are the semi-local unipotent orbital functions. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.TwistedBruhat.exists_forall_integral_transversal_tracePushforward_eq_indicator_prod_twistedLocalFactor_unram`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.TwistedBruhat.exists_forall_integral_transversal_tracePushforward_eq_indicator_prod_twistedLocalFactor_unram), where the push-forward along the trace is applied afterwards.
